While implementing the ratings feature, all endpoints returned 404 Not Found even though the routes were correctly defined in routes/ratings.py with ratings_bp = Blueprint('ratings', __name__). The issue was that I forgot to register the blueprint in the app factory, so Flask did not recognize any of the routes. After adding app.register_blueprint(ratings_bp), the endpoints worked and returned 201 Created as expected. This showed that defining routes is not enough — they must be explicitly wired into the application to exist at runtime.
